# a hidden subunit whose C implementation links a library nothing can link
# (lazyalias/nativec.zd, a link for this subunit). Its parent re-exports a
# type from it, and the program never names that re-export -- so a compiler
# that resolves the alias to classify it reaches the subunit and links a
# library that does not exist, and one that resolves on demand never does.

Thing: record {
    n: i64
}

# probe -- a native, so the subunit is one its parent's implementation speaks for
probe: function out i64 is native
